welcome to max tech and this is our  review of the iPhone 11 pro in this  review I'm not gonna tell you that the  iPhone 11 pro is the best iPhone ever  made it obviously is I'm also not gonna  bore you with all the specs that you've  heard a thousand times already what I'm  gonna talk about are the things that  actually matter to both attack  enthusiasts like myself and an average  consumer like my wife both of us have  been using the iPhone 11 pro for a few  days now so I've collected my own  thoughts and I also interviewed my wife  to see what differences she noticed in  what she liked about her iPhone 11 Pro  but before I get into that let's first  talk about what happened at Apple's  event there's no doubt that a lot of  people were disappointed they argue that  Apple shouldn't have used the name Pro  since it's missing a few Pro features  like 120 Hertz refresh rate a USB C port  in reverse wireless charging but after  people started to get their hands on the  iPhone 11 Pro the disappointment started  to fade away so the question is does it  matter that the new iPhone is missing a  few Pro features that Apple fans were  anticipating well for most people not  really what it does pack is a few very  important features and changes that make  it a seriously good package overall in  terms of being a premium smartphone it  now packs all three camera lenses that  you'd hope to see in a smartphone  including a new night mode feature which  as you'll see later works incredibly  well it packs the best processor in any  smartphone  it has top-of-the-line battery life a  high quality display that's even  brighter this year incredibly balanced  speakers and it finally comes with a  fast charger in the box it packs  top-of-the-line security and it features  a truly unique design that you'll never  confuse for anything else it seems as  though for the first time in a very long  time the iPhone 11 pro gives you a  complete package of features and that's  what truly matters  [Music]  when it comes to upgrading your iPhone I  thought of a formula for iPhones  upgradability that is more realistic for  regular consumers and offering a full  package of features that work very well  together is the first piece of the  puzzle  second the iPhone has to look and feel  different not that many people upgraded  from the iPhone 10 to the 10s and that's  because it looked basically identical to  the 10 only the tennis max look  different because it was obviously much  larger and that's actually the flagship  model that most people upgraded to this  year the iPhone 11 probe looks and feels  way different with a brand new unique  feeling matte glass back a relocated  Apple logo the new popular midnight  green color and most importantly a very  unique square camera bump with large  triple camera lenses that really stand  out that new square bump with three  lenses has become a trademark alongside  the pro branding so now it's almost  impossible to mistake the 11pro for the  iPhone 10 or 10s unless you're looking  at the front of course the third thing  that matters is that it sounds different  and having the word Pro in the name is  more unique than ever before when I was  standing in line at the Apple store on  launch day I kept hearing regular people  saying that they want the new iPhone Pro  they seemed like they didn't really know  that much about tech but what they did  know is that they wanted the pro model  and throughout the weekend I kept  hearing people ask is that the new Pro  is that the iPhone Pro it seems as  though the 11-part of the name has faded  away under the success of the pro name  so it seems like using pro is already  working for apples benefit even if some  people disagree with it before I get  into my personal thoughts on what truly  matters about the iPhone 11 Pro and Pro  Macs as well as the downsides or  disappointments of the pro I want to  quickly mention the real-world  differences and changes my wife noticed  and enjoyed about her new 11 pro first  off she loves the camera especially the  new wider angle on the selfie cam  allowing her to fit more into the frame  without having to stretch her hand out  as far as she can she also absolutely  the new ultra wide lens and she had a  blast taking unique and creative photos  at the park she was also really  impressed with the video stabilization  and she actually really likes the square  bump on the back  compared to her old tennis Max's  vertical bump and she noticed much  better battery life as well in terms of  performance she didn't really notice the  difference coming from the 10s but she  doesn't really do any heavy tasks like  gaming or using professional apps or  anything like that so overall she's very  happy with their new iPhone 11 pro even  coming from the 10s so I think regular  consumers who are coming from an older  iPhone will definitely notice a  difference now let's get into the  real-world differences that I a tech  enthusiast noticed after spending a few  days with the iPhone 11 pro max first of  all I'm pleasantly surprised with the  battery life every time I check it I'd  be surprised at how high it was compared  to my old tennis max and on Sunday I was  at 61% battery life after coming home at  9:30 p.m. this has never happened on my  tennis max so I think the battery life  is perhaps the biggest deal on the new  iPhone 11 Pro and don't take my word for  it mister who's the boss just released  his battery drain test and even the  smaller iPhone 11 Pro beat out the note  10 plus and that was with the note  manually set to a lower resolution than  both of the iPhones at 1080p instead of  the 1440p the note is capable of and the  iPhone 11 pro max lasted 8 hours and 32  minutes the best battery life mister  who's the boss has ever seen on any  smartphone as far as the design I  seriously can't get enough of it the  matte finish on the glass feels  incredible in the hand and I'm shocked  at how Apple is able to pull off the  square bump on the back it just looks so  unique in premium compared to the  vertical bump on the 10s and so far  everyone else I know loves the new look  the speakers have also been improved  from the 10s max with the top and bottom  speakers being much more balanced than  before which is why I think the new  spatial audio sound effect works so well  as far as performance I honestly haven't  noticed a difference in the UI and using  the phone normally but what most people  don't really think about is that the  reason the cameras are as good as they  are is solely because of the extra  performance of the  13 Bionic chip in the 11pro that's where  most of the improvements are going and  I'll talk about them in just a minute  and even though a lot of the  improvements are geared towards  efficiency for getting that awesome  battery life we actually saw a huge  improvement in raw performance in both  processor and graphics workloads for  gaming the iPhone 10s had excellent  performance being able to max out the  graphics on basically any game we tried  but it had a huge issue while playing  fortnight at high brightness at 60  frames per second after only 10 minutes  the 10s would heat up and the display  would greatly dim so I tried it on the  11pro max and it was able to last much  longer before dimming and it didn't dim  nearly as much as before so I'm really  impressed with the efficiency of the new  a 13 chip  especially since you'll get better  battery life during long gaming sessions  in my opinion even if you can't notice  the difference in performance right now  having the extra power of the a 13 chip  for the next couple of years is going to  be a big deal from when new apps and  games come out that'll actually be able  to use that performance and now let's  get into the cameras the main upgrade  this year we now get the ultra wide lens  which is actually really fun to use the  quality isn't nearly as good as the wide  lens but it's a blast to get unique  angles and shots the wide lens looks  better than ever with excellent dynamic  range and image quality and I'm glad the  Apple added a bit more contrast to the  photos so they don't look as flat as  last year's 10s and the white balance  looks very consistent between lenses  whereas last year it leaned towards the  warm side far too often and for the  telephoto lens I've actually noticed  that photos taken with this lens turned  out better with less noise especially  for portrait mode photos however I'm  quite disappointed with portrait blur  edging I thought they did improve on  this this year but it still sucks when  it comes to missing large sections of  the background so I really hope Apple  adds a time-of-flight sensor next year  perhaps the biggest deal is Apple moving  from 7 megapixels to 12 on the  front-facing camera as well as making  the lens wider in general it's much more  detailed than before and being able to  record 4k 60fps selfie video is insane  and finally Apple has added a night mode  and it does such a great job as  actually since the colors turn out  natural and not oversaturated like on a  lot of other Android phones the only  downside is that you can't use night  mode with the ultra wide lens or the  selfie camera which is a huge bummer as  for video recording Apple has completely  knocked it out of the park with the  11pro the quality looks incredible and  beats out basically every other phone on  the market and this year the  stabilization is absolutely phenomenal  it just works so incredibly well in  Aleppo you can also record with the  ultra wide lens but the biggest  improvement for video recording comes  thanks to the a13 Bionic chip you can  now shoot at 4k 60 while getting  extended dynamic range which means that  the chip is actually recording 4k 120  with 60 darker frames and 60 brighter  frames being blended together in real  time to offer incredible dynamic range  this is a huge deal and it puts an even  bigger gap between it and other  smartphones however there's also a  really big downside with recording while  shooting in 4k 60 you can't switch  between lenses that means if you start  recording with the ultra wide lens you  can't zoom out or switch to another lens  it works perfectly fine while recording  at 30fps but not at 60 that's a major  flaw especially now that we have the  added ultra wide lens but overall the  cameras are outstanding on the 11pro and  we'll be putting out some very detailed  camera comparison shortly so if you're  not already subscribed make sure to do  that right now so you don't miss out on  those videos so that leads me into a few  things that I found extremely  disappointing this year yes the 11pro  offers the most complete  iPhone package we've seen in years and I  honestly think that most people who are  on the edge of upgrading should just do  it unless they're perfectly happy with  their current device but if we had these  three things I honestly think it would  be perfect  first off the same 4 gigabytes of RAM on  the 11pro  that's just a bit sad and even worse the  same 64 gigabytes of storage at the base  price is just embarrassing especially  since the note 10 plus comes with 256  gigabytes of even faster storage at the  same base price and finally I was really  hoping for an always-on display on the  11pro as  actually since Apple added it to their  new series five Apple watch but we still  don't have it on the iPhone other than  that the iPhone 11 Pro is an excellent  package overall and it looks and feels  more premium than ever before making the  $1000 price honestly seem worth it again  just like it was with the iPhone 10 from  two years ago this has been vadim with  max TAC and if you enjoyed this review  make sure to check out some of our other  videos right over there and click that  circle above to subscribe so you don't  miss out on our upcoming camera  comparisons thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next one  [Music]
 

